---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Race from '../components/site/Race.astro';
import { measuredOn, ratio, workloads } from '../lib/bench';

// The median pass of the roles workload, per host, from the performance page of the documentation.
const roles = [
  ['Opening the connections', 172.6, ''],
  ['file ×8, lineinfile ×8, stat ×5', 52.8, 'native'],
  ['systemd, 3 tasks', 52.4, 'native'],
  ['setup, gathering facts', 47.6, 'native'],
  ['apt, 8 tasks', 38.4, 'native'],
  ['Frames and blobs on the wire', 27.1, ''],
  ['Preparing tasks on the controller', 25.0, ''],
  ['Building the Python module set', 15.3, 'cached'],
  ['Waiting for the other host', 10.6, ''],
] as const;
const k3s = [
  ['Restarting k3s, server and agent', 13032, 'native systemd'],
  ['service_facts', 2485, 'native'],
  ['apt with update_cache', 2205, 'Python'],
  ['Opening the connections', 350, ''],
  ['Waiting for the other host', 253, ''],
  ['Preparing tasks on the controller', 185, ''],
  ['package_facts', 168, 'native'],
  ['Gathering facts', 55, 'native'],
  ['Building the Python module set', 30.6, 'cached'],
] as const;

const config = [
  ['Managed hosts', 'two Ubuntu 24.04 hosts, 4 cores each'],
  ['Controller', 'Ubuntu 26.04, 8 cores'],
  ['Volant', 'release build, default settings: native modules on, one SSH connection per host'],
  ['Reference', 'ansible-core 2.19.12 with pipelining = True, forks at its default of 5'],
  ['Passes', 'one warm-up pass per engine, then three timed passes each; the median is reported'],
  ['Check', 'every pass must end on the same PLAY RECAP under both engines, or the recipe fails'],
];
const max = (rows: readonly (readonly [string, number, string])[]) => Math.max(...rows.map((r) => r[1]));
const ms = (v: number) => (v >= 1000 ? `${(v / 1000).toFixed(2)} s` : `${v} ms`);
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Performance"
  description="Two real workloads measured against ansible-core 2.19.12 with pipelining, the configuration behind them, and the commands that reproduce them."
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Measured on real playbooks.</h1>
    <p>
      Two workloads, each run by a recipe in the repository, against ansible-core 2.19.12 with pipelining turned on.
      Every figure on this page comes from those recipes, measured on {measuredOn}.
    </p>
    <div class="ratios">
      {
        workloads.map((w) => (
          <div>
            <b class="mono">{ratio(w).toFixed(ratio(w) > 10 ? 0 : 2)}×</b>
            <span>faster on {w.name.toLowerCase()}</span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Race />
      <p class="why">
        The ratios are far apart for a reason. The roles change nothing on a converged host, so almost all of the
        reference’s time goes to the machinery around each module. The k3s playbook restarts services and runs install
        scripts on every pass, and that work takes as long under either engine.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2>Where Volant spends its time.</h2>
        <p>The median pass, split by step. A native step is answered in Rust by the agent on the host.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="splits">
        {
          [
            { title: 'Four Galaxy roles', total: '0.529 s for two hosts', rows: roles },
            { title: 'k3s-ansible, the server', total: '23.477 s for two hosts', rows: k3s },
          ].map((group) => (
            <figure class="panel reveal">
              <div class="core split-core">
                <figcaption>
                  <b>{group.title}</b>
                  <span>{group.total}</span>
                </figcaption>
                {group.rows.map(([label, value, kind]) => (
                  <div class="row">
                    <span class="label">
                      {label}
                      {kind && <em>{kind}</em>}
                    </span>
                    <span class="bar">
                      <i style={`--w: ${(value / max(group.rows)) * 100}%`} class:list={{ native: kind.startsWith('native') }} />
                    </span>
                    <span class="value mono">{ms(value)}</span>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </figure>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p class="why reveal">
        On k3s, most of the 23.5 seconds is work the playbook asks for: restarting the k3s service, running its install
        script and 13 <code>command</code> tasks. Both engines pay for those the same way, because they are processes on
        the host. <a class="text-link" href="/docs/project/performance/#what-is-left">What is left</a> explains the rest.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap two">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2>The configuration.</h2>
        <p>Default settings on both sides, except pipelining, which makes the reference faster.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="config reveal">
        {
          config.map(([name, value]) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{name}</dt>
              <dd>{value}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap two">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2>Reproduce them.</h2>
        <p>
          Both recipes build Volant in release mode, run against the hosts you name and print the medians and the ratio.
          They change the hosts they run on, so use machines you can wipe.
        </p>
        <p>
          On your own playbook, <code>--profile</code> prints the same split for your run.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel reveal">
        <pre class="code core"><span class="c"># ansible-core 2.19.12 installed with uv tool install,
# and sudo without a password on both hosts</span>
VOLANT_TARGET_HOST=host1 VOLANT_SECOND_HOST=host2 <span class="k">just bench 3</span>
VOLANT_TARGET_HOST=host1 VOLANT_SECOND_HOST=host2 <span class="k">just bench-k3s 3</span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="why reveal">
        These figures describe two playbooks on two hosts. Yours depend on your network, on what your tasks do, on how
        many of them a native module covers and on how many hosts you drive at once.
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/project/performance/">The full measurement</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .ratios {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 3.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .ratios div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.2rem;
  }
  .ratios b {
    color: var(--brand-hi);
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5vw, 3.6rem);
    font-weight: 560;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .ratios span {
    color: var(--fg-3);
  }
  .why {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    color: var(--fg-2);
  }
  .splits {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
  }
  .splits figure {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .split-core {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }
  figcaption {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  figcaption span {
    color: var(--fg-3);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }
  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(0, 1fr) 4.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .label {
    color: var(--fg-2);
  }
  .label em {
    margin-inline-start: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--fg-4);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }
  .bar {
    height: 0.5rem;
  }
  .bar i {
    display: block;
    width: var(--w);
    min-width: 2px;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--fg-4);
  }
  .bar i.native {
    background: var(--brand);
  }
  .value {
    color: var(--fg);
    text-align: end;
  }
  .two {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .two .section-head p + p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .config {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .config div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 9rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 0.8rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .config dt {
    font-weight: 560;
  }
  .config dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-2);
  }
  @media (max-width: 60rem) {
    .splits,
    .two {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 36rem) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 4.5rem;
    }
    .bar {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      grid-row: 2;
    }
    .config div {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0.2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
